id: pm-graph-jrc0
title: Adopt pm CLI and SDK 2026.8.7 with a covered TypeScript merge-driver lifecycle
description: Bring pm-graph onto the current pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog release while replacing the authored JavaScript prepare hook with erasable TypeScript that preserves PATH semantics and safely installs merge drivers on POSIX and Windows.
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[5]: compatibility,pm-sdk,tdd,typescript,windows
created_at: "2026-08-07T18:45:28.229Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T19:33:50.259Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T19:33:50.243Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T19:33:50.243Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Peer and development dependencies target pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.7 and pm-changelog 2026.8.7; pm merge install writes the current managed merge-driver fence; The prepare lifecycle is authored only in erasable TypeScript and preserves POSIX and Windows PATH resolution; Absent pm exits cleanly while a present broken pm fails loudly; Lifecycle source has real behavior-driven 100/100/100 coverage; npm and Bun release gates and fresh packed-artifact acceptance pass; Privacy/history and review evidence is recorded without publishing
definition_of_ready: Canonical checkout is clean; no duplicate item or open PR exists; current hook semantics and installed dependency drift are understood.
value: "Keeps pm-graph installable and conflict-safe for agents across npm, Bun, POSIX, and Windows."
outcome: A packed pm-graph artifact installs against pm 2026.8.7 and its lifecycle behavior is exact-covered without silent broken-CLI failures.
why_now: The fleet compatibility campaign requires the current SDK and canonical multi-agent merge fence before further feature work.
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Updated pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog to 2026.8.7, installed the canonical merge fence, migrated the lifecycle to erasable TypeScript, added host-independent path resolution and a real Windows process-boundary gate, and resolved all actionable review findings."
expected_result: "Current dependencies, conflict-safe merge configuration, fail-loud cross-platform lifecycle behavior, exact lifecycle coverage, npm/Bun release gates, fresh packed-artifact acceptance, and exact-head reviews all pass without publication."
actual_result: "All bounded criteria passed: 205 Linux tests plus exact 12-test lifecycle coverage, real Windows cmd.exe acceptance, zero production vulnerabilities, deterministic package/changelog checks, fresh installed-pm graph acceptance, green CI/security checks, and no remaining actionable review findings. Full-source quality and historical privacy remain separate P0 blockers."
notes[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T19:02:08.411Z",codex,"Fresh packed-artifact acceptance against installed pm 2026.8.7 activated all 15 command paths plus exporter and output-format service capabilities,created real tracker data,returned version 2026.8.7 from ping,exported the graph,and passed pm validate without warnings."
  "2026-08-07T19:02:08.411Z",codex,"npm and Bun release gates passed with 205 tests and zero skips. The lifecycle source reports exact 100 percent lines,branches,and functions; the broader src/index.ts remains 83.13/78.54/89.66 and is independently blocked by pm-graph-fjfn."
  "2026-08-07T19:02:08.411Z",codex,"Reachable-history evidence confirms pm-graph-xc7g remains a publication blocker: non-approved identities and host-specific paths exist in historical commits. No npm publication was attempted."
  "2026-08-07T19:08:41.553Z",codex,"Greptile P2 was valid: deterministic runner assertions do not prove cmd.exe parser behavior. Added a Windows-only real-process fixture whose shim path contains spaces and a literal percent-delimited segment,plus a windows-latest CI job where npm ci executes the production prepare lifecycle."
  "2026-08-07T19:15:42.201Z",codex,"CodeRabbit findings were valid and fixed: resolver path splitting/joining now uses the explicit target platform APIs rather than host defaults,and real default-filesystem fixtures are portable across POSIX and Windows hosts. Targeted coverage remains exact 100/100/100 with 12 tests and zero skips."
  "2026-08-07T19:33:49.863Z",codex,"Exact head b59f7d8 passed Node 22,Node 26,windows-latest real cmd.exe lifecycle,Semgrep,DeepScan,Hound,and Greptile 5/5. CodeRabbit completed an exact-head re-review with no actionable defects; Sourcery and Cubic remained quota-unavailable and Gemini remained silent."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T18:51:02.281Z",codex,Windows cmd must receive the resolved shim path through an environment variable with delayed expansion disabled; embedding a path containing spaces or percent-delimited segments in command text is unsafe.
